WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:12.500
In April 2023, Mr Guo, who runs a technology company in Fuzhou, China, got a WeChat video call from a friend.

2
00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:23.090
The friend said an acquaintance needed a 4.3 million yuan deposit for a bid, and asked to pass it through Mr Guo's company account.

3
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:35.280
On the video, it was the friend's face, and the friend's voice. Without checking whether any money had arrived, Mr Guo sent the 4.3 million.

4
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:48.230
Later he phoned his friend, who said he knew nothing about it. Police in Baotou reported that a scammer had used AI face-swapping to pose as the friend.

5
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:56.700
Mr Guo said afterwards: I confirmed the face and the voice on the video, so I let my guard down.

6
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:03.660
This is C5: safety, privacy, and how to avoid scams.

7
00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:10.530
You'll learn how to guard against fake faces and fake voices, and what not to give to AI.

8
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:23.220
From someone's photos, videos and recordings, AI can synthesise how they look and sound. This is called deep synthesis: face-swapping and voice cloning.

9
00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:37.890
The raw material a scammer needs is your face and your voice. Financial regulators in China warn that scammers pose as customer service, recruiters or dates to collect your voice and face.

10
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:47.560
America's consumer protection agency warns, too: with just a short recording, a scammer can clone a family member's voice.

11
00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:54.670
So remember: seeing isn't necessarily believing, and neither is hearing.

12
00:01:55.467 --> 00:01:58.707
These scams often have a few things in common.

13
00:01:59.057 --> 00:02:05.737
One: they want money, and fast. I've had a car accident; I urgently need a deposit.

14
00:02:06.087 --> 00:02:12.327
Two: only one channel. Only on this video call, only on this number.

15
00:02:12.677 --> 00:02:18.037
Three: they want secrecy. Whatever you do, don't tell Mum and Dad.

16
00:02:18.387 --> 00:02:25.547
Four: they want you to pay in ways that are hard to get back, like wire transfers or gift cards.

17
00:02:25.897 --> 00:02:31.217
When you see these signs, stop, and don't rush to send money.

18
00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:38.600
So what do you do? Don't rely on your eyes or your ears. Follow a routine.

19
00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:46.110
Whenever money is involved, hang up, and call back on the number saved in your own phone.

20
00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:57.750
China's Ministry of Public Security warns: for any transfer, check again through contact details you already have, and never trust a single video call.

21
00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:05.980
You can also agree a code word with your family that only you know. If the caller can't say it, be careful.

22
00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:16.210
If you're unsure, call the anti-fraud line: in China, 96110; elsewhere, your local police or anti-fraud line.

23
00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:27.280
Now, when we use AI ourselves. Chinese state security authorities warn that AI tools collect and store what you type in.

24
00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:40.670
So don't give AI your ID number, bank card number, passwords or verification codes; and don't casually upload photos or recordings of yourself and your family.

25
00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:52.220
Medical records, other people's private details, work documents: remove the names and just describe the situation, or don't paste the original at all.

26
00:03:52.570 --> 00:03:58.730
In one line: treat whatever you give AI as something others might see.

27
00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:11.100
There's also a new rule in China: since 1 September 2025, AI-generated text, images, audio and video must be labelled.

28
00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:20.770
An AI-generated label tells you it's synthetic. But no label doesn't mean it's real: scammers don't label their fake videos.

29
00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:27.120
And when you make images or videos with AI yourself, label them when you post them.

30
00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:43.700
Remember: three red lines, one phone call. Money, health and personal information: check first. Hang up, call back on a number you saved, and if you're unsure, call the anti-fraud line.

31
00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:51.690
A small exercise: today, agree a family code word, and practise hanging up and calling back.

32
00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:57.040
Next time, C6: fairness, ethics and work.
